{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/playwright.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:52:29.357153Z","id":"f3a0d4529a01c427646a27543d5937df8ac944304a4082542ab253691ae75bae","body":{"detail":"Playwright runs Chromium projects only (web/playwright.config.ts:31-36), and the e2e stand-in (web/e2e/app-scheme.ts) plays Android's https://app.clax.invalid origins. The Apple app's clax://app and clax://<id>.c origins are covered by unit tests only (web/shell/src/transport.test.ts \"the transport on Apple's origins (clax:)\", web/shell/src/origin.test.ts, web/shell/src/socket-url.test.ts, web/shell/src/view/live-layers.test.ts), which cannot show what WebKit does with a non-special scheme: location.origin \"null\", URL parsing of clax: URLs, the content policy naming clax: sources, and fetch of /api on a custom scheme.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"eb6186615828e562406e756aa40ae2033bf220ad0cd70f70d10e40d05da8068b"},"suggested_fix":"Add a WebKit Playwright project that serves the stand-in on clax: origins (WebKit has no route for a custom scheme, so this needs a WKURLSchemeHandler-like stand-in, or a run inside the macOS app's integration tests).","summary":"The app's Apple path (clax:// shell and content origins under WebKit) never runs in a browser test","tags":["review","app-mode","testing","revisit:when the e2e suite gains a WebKit project or the macOS app gains WebView integration tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/package.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:28:58.613424Z","id":"4b80b7168f667e2561d1e854c4f501a4cf83b61b61a57904321a506c0266eb33","body":{"detail":"Comparing dist/markdown-it.mjs of 15.0.2 (bazel-bin/web/node_modules/markdown-it) with `npm pack markdown-it@15.0.3`: the `reference` block rule is rewritten with a MAX_LABEL_LENGTH bound and the `html_inline` rule's regex replaced by a linear `scanSpecial`, both quadratic-time fixes; the rest is bracing. markdown.ts disables `reference` and sets `html: false`, so neither path runs here today. The lock's integrity hashes for markdown-it, linkify-it, mdurl, uc.micro, punycode.js, entities and argparse match `npm view <pkg> dist.integrity`.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"570fbbea35388549f473a7df906c57e49582c95ef11c785f721b6f9c8d8d0caf"},"suggested_fix":"Move to 15.0.3 (and the lock), then `just bazel-sync`.","summary":"markdown-it 15.0.3 (2026-10-16) is out; 15.0.2 is pinned","tags":["review","review:comment-markdown-115cb94","supply-chain","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/package.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:30:45.671538Z","id":"9e1e7eacf93597d0a6fa07f8df9844ff6676b41b553b98ecb7d32680a9ec4c66","body":{"detail":"web/package.json:36 `\"markdown-it\": \"15.0.2\"`. `npm view markdown-it time --json` lists \"15.0.3\": \"2026-10-16T01:25:15.267Z\". Diffing bazel-bin/web/node_modules/markdown-it/dist/markdown-it.mjs against `npm pack markdown-it@15.0.3` package/dist/markdown-it.mjs shows added `var MAX_LABEL_LENGTH = 999;` and `function scanSpecial(state, pos)`; markdown.ts:71 disables `reference` and sets `html: false`, so the suggestion kind fits.","kind":"comment","references":"4b80b7168f667e2561d1e854c4f501a4cf83b61b61a57904321a506c0266eb33","summary":"confirmed: 15.0.3 is published and adds the label bound and scanSpecial; 15.0.2 is pinned","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/package.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:50:00.843973Z","id":"a43d6022a4850fc982bf0efd0d51171a91e187752e1077d318bd3ff5b95cc802","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1ddf1738e","summary":"Fixed in 1ddf1738e: markdown-it 15.0.3 (published 2026-10-16) in package.json and the lock; `npm pack markdown-it@15.0.3 | openssl dgst -sha512 -binary | base64` gives +Az7Ojz3iRGu8KYMvJ6xVhvrxP3eE+vEtJX75Ow88XBpcQNV/0lGX5ZynIIBftREo4DC2jsveAMDaeltmm8QvQ==, the lock's integrity; `just bazel-sync` changed no derived file; //web:unit, //web:typecheck and //web:bundle_size passed at 7a1df0ce2.","supersedes":"4b80b7168f667e2561d1e854c4f501a4cf83b61b61a57904321a506c0266eb33","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/playwright.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:43:10.915211Z","id":"f5abbe96626871d272d202170127c74fa24a5c40cfecc7f5ed6ee29d3525b2ae","body":{"detail":"Every expectation that does not set its own timeout fails after 5 s, so on a machine with a load average far above its cores a page load or reload plus render can fail a test whose condition would have held. web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts (WAIT_MS 90 s) and web/e2e/linked.spec.ts (60 s) configure longer waits for themselves; the rest of the suite does not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"459473ab28b845f2bfe5688c7f074fb7c3abe27fbb4d6e7e56ae3e122503069e"},"summary":"The suite's 5 s expect timeout decides outcomes on a loaded machine","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/vite.overlay.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295857Z","id":"298da2c54a944450357d9913d63967ed2f7faa77a4402daedadbd0d186d84584","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures the bridge, the transport, the shell entries and the extension, not the overlay, so its size can grow unseen. One IIFE cannot load the clip renderer lazily the way the bridge loads its parts.","kind":"concern","suggested_fix":"Add an overlay entry to bundle-size.mjs's sizes (gz(\"_clax/overlay.js\")) and its budget to web/perf/bundle-budget.json.","summary":"dist/_clax/overlay.js (about 50 KB gzip, 139 KB raw, most of it modern-screenshot) has no budget in web/perf/bundle-budget.json","tags":["overlay","bundle-budget","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/vite.overlay.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T14:05:58.516330Z","id":"d968db904f3108376318c0f441b0106f2e0051bdf7b53423b226a67822ed76e1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f93d25e1c","summary":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs now measures dist/_clax/overlay.js as overlay (printed as embed) and refuses an overlay.mjs that imports another file; web/perf/bundle-budget.json gives it 78082 (measured 70984 plus 10 percent); web/scripts/bundle-size.test.ts covers the budget and the import check. bazel test //web:bundle_size //web:unit PASSED at f93d25e1c.","supersedes":"298da2c54a944450357d9913d63967ed2f7faa77a4402daedadbd0d186d84584","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/tsconfig.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T02:30:26.227935Z","id":"0b59dcaa22534a85b0741056f8a075de026584477e73f9f6801f9db5f5d44f3a","body":{"detail":"The include list has no demo/: //web:typecheck reaches demo/lib/worker.ts, seed.ts and http.ts only through web/e2e/hosted-demo*.spec.ts, which import them. The runners themselves (just hosted-demo, just clax-dev-local) run under Node's type stripping, which drops types without checking them, so a type error there shows only when that line runs. A tsc pass over them with @types/node (target ES2023, module NodeNext, allowImportingTsExtensions) found none on 2026-10-28; adding demo to this include, or a //demo:typecheck target, would keep it so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"ce42848e773d2d81d76b6d4138fae3fc8f68a748d4fbd5db702c76c6aa6e6cc6"},"summary":"No gate typechecks demo/local.ts, demo/clax-dev-local.ts, demo/agents.ts or demo/lib/build.ts","tags":["ci","demo","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/playwright.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:36.794003Z","id":"4bf32ede04ca25183bd1af4d9e18636b7891238fa62191a23f3e498cf4ea4a9b","body":{"detail":"Every expectation that does not set its own timeout fails after 5 s, so on a machine with a load average far above its cores a page load or reload plus render can fail a test whose condition would have held. web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts (WAIT_MS 90 s) and web/e2e/linked.spec.ts (60 s) configure longer waits for themselves; the rest of the suite does not.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":27},"content_hash":"459473ab28b845f2bfe5688c7f074fb7c3abe27fbb4d6e7e56ae3e122503069e"},"summary":"The suite's 5 s expect timeout decides outcomes on a loaded machine","supersedes":"f5abbe96626871d272d202170127c74fa24a5c40cfecc7f5ed6ee29d3525b2ae","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/playwright.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:56.579578Z","id":"dbd6eda2fa26e876b12aa406a34cbda555e866738e196fe3443ce4d529595b68","body":{"detail":"Playwright runs Chromium projects only (web/playwright.config.ts:31-36), and the e2e stand-in (web/e2e/app-scheme.ts) plays Android's https://app.clax.invalid origins. The Apple app's clax://app and clax://<id>.c origins are covered by unit tests only (web/shell/src/transport.test.ts \"the transport on Apple's origins (clax:)\", web/shell/src/origin.test.ts, web/shell/src/socket-url.test.ts, web/shell/src/view/live-layers.test.ts), which cannot show what WebKit does with a non-special scheme: location.origin \"null\", URL parsing of clax: URLs, the content policy naming clax: sources, and fetch of /api on a custom scheme.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":39},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"8bfc543adb794b39e6dc557daaecc32db867edbdcb727df0a554100438554821"},"suggested_fix":"Add a WebKit Playwright project that serves the stand-in on clax: origins (WebKit has no route for a custom scheme, so this needs a WKURLSchemeHandler-like stand-in, or a run inside the macOS app's integration tests).","summary":"The app's Apple path (clax:// shell and content origins under WebKit) never runs in a browser test","supersedes":"f3a0d4529a01c427646a27543d5937df8ac944304a4082542ab253691ae75bae","tags":["review","app-mode","testing","revisit:when the e2e suite gains a WebKit project or the macOS app gains WebView integration tests","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.501196Z","id":"cbb32bfbb00e1fc31ab3967cc5fa8ac0ff3f4cf284d4cd2a63da298543f4fdee","body":{"detail":"web/package.json:8 appends `node scripts/build-sdk.mjs` to `pnpm run build`, and //web:dist_all (web/BUILD.bazel:95-114) is that one action with dist-sdk among its out_dirs. //web:dist and //web:dist_extension are picked from the same action, so building the web UI for the binary also runs the SDK's Vite build and its TypeScript declaration emit, and a failure only the package has (a newly bundled npm package with no license file, build-sdk.mjs:110-111; a declaration TypeScript cannot emit, build-sdk.mjs:130-132; a bundled Clax file outside web/bridge, web/overlay and web/sdk, build-sdk.mjs:100-103) fails the clax build. The e2e web build is already its own action (//web:dist_e2e, `pnpm run build:e2e`).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":95},"end":{"line":114},"content_hash":"cdf086d85ea1cd842653ad07943214b9b7b19a96925fc2a93096319a65784582"},"suggested_fix":"Leave `build` as it was and give the package its own npm_script_build running `build:sdk` (out_dirs dist-sdk), as //web:dist_e2e does; `just web` can still build both targets.","summary":"The SDK package builds inside //web:dist_all, so every web build the clax binary embeds now runs it and fails when it fails","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","bazel","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.339312Z","id":"891b2130bca1424405627f49efd8670f10f16959e49171d2371eb115a13d70f0","body":{"detail":"web/package.json:8 ends `build` with `&& node scripts/build-sdk.mjs` (added on this branch; `git diff main...HEAD -- web/package.json`). web/BUILD.bazel:97-114 npm_script_build dist_all runs script \"build\" with out_dirs dist, dist-extension, dist-extension-test, dist-sdk; :dist (116-121) and :dist_sdk (138-143) are pick_dirs of it. //web:dist is a data input of crates/clax-server/BUILD.bazel:34, crates/clax-mcp/BUILD.bazel:9 and crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel:13,94,119. The cited failure paths exist: build-sdk.mjs:111 (no license file), 130-132 (declaration diagnostics), 100-103 (Clax file outside web/bridge, overlay, sdk). //web:dist_e2e is its own action at web/BUILD.bazel:146-156 (`build:e2e`). Line citations correct.","kind":"comment","references":"cbb32bfbb00e1fc31ab3967cc5fa8ac0ff3f4cf284d4cd2a63da298543f4fdee","summary":"confirmed: build-sdk.mjs runs inside pnpm run build, the one //web:dist_all action that //web:dist is picked from","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:12.319243Z","id":"e92469ee81c2f50f798c111805202e2a5076519110ce2d5699c8fcb490511a48","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2eeec0bf","summary":"web/package.json's `build` no longer runs build-sdk.mjs; //web:dist_sdk is its own npm_script_build running `build:sdk` (web/BUILD.bazel), and the native paths (just web-native, quality_gates.sh lane_web, just perf-native) run `pnpm run build:sdk` before reading web/dist-sdk. `just web` built them as separate actions ('NpmScript web/dist-sdk', 'NpmScript web/dist'); `just web-test` passed //web:lint, :typecheck, :unit, :bundle_size and :sdk_package (Bazel); bash scripts/run.test.sh: 'all run.sh checks passed'.","supersedes":"cbb32bfbb00e1fc31ab3967cc5fa8ac0ff3f4cf284d4cd2a63da298543f4fdee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:20:15.815392Z","id":"df40661a0f873ad6c311de5173d9d59438544256717a3bfbbaaab49e87b2fc66","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:87c52fbf5aba19b0fe798b12083a46a340a05fd0","summary":"web/package.json's `build` no longer runs build-sdk.mjs; //web:dist_sdk is its own npm_script_build running `build:sdk` (web/BUILD.bazel), and the native paths (just web-native, quality_gates.sh lane_web, just perf-native) run `pnpm run build:sdk` before reading web/dist-sdk. `just web` built them as separate actions ('NpmScript web/dist-sdk', 'NpmScript web/dist'); `just web-test` passed //web:lint, :typecheck, :unit, :bundle_size and :sdk_package (Bazel); bash scripts/run.test.sh: 'all run.sh checks passed'.","supersedes":"e92469ee81c2f50f798c111805202e2a5076519110ce2d5699c8fcb490511a48","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T16:31:03.449479Z","id":"02c1e4c9eaeb14a301e05433600fccdee7962d54f9b4b6f10581ef9dab098a94","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0c62fd9c188159d61763262e901f93c4f45458f2","summary":"web/package.json's `build` no longer runs build-sdk.mjs; //web:dist_sdk is its own npm_script_build running `build:sdk` (web/BUILD.bazel), and the native paths (just web-native, quality_gates.sh lane_web, just perf-native) run `pnpm run build:sdk` before reading web/dist-sdk. `just web` built them as separate actions ('NpmScript web/dist-sdk', 'NpmScript web/dist'); `just web-test` passed //web:lint, :typecheck, :unit, :bundle_size and :sdk_package (Bazel); bash scripts/run.test.sh: 'all run.sh checks passed'.","supersedes":"df40661a0f873ad6c311de5173d9d59438544256717a3bfbbaaab49e87b2fc66","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T19:56:47.896442Z","id":"b9e393f8335c7beb5df7ab38931734e4701593f06f10f0114498596b79af3dd8","body":{"detail":"The npm_script_build takes `:files_app`, the copy of every APP_DIRS directory (shell/**, bridge/**, extension/**, contract/**, scripts/**, quickstart/**, sdk/**, overlay/**; web/BUILD.bazel:23-31). The package reads only web/sdk, web/overlay and web/bridge, plus build-sdk.mjs, extension-clean.mjs, overlay-component-css.mjs, tsconfig.json, svelte.config.js and package.json. Any edit under web/shell therefore invalidates //web:dist_sdk, //web:sdk_package and //web:bundle_size. And a stray import of web/shell from overlay source is caught only by build-sdk.mjs's license guard at build time, not by the sandbox.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":152},"content_hash":"e78aa8d6e477d5acac0c4612cfe97f77a9bf983dcf68c2de5a907b28f7b48459"},"suggested_fix":"Add a `copy_to_bin` group `files_sdk` (sdk/**, overlay/** and bridge/** minus tests, the three scripts and the config files above) and give //web:dist_sdk only that. The sandbox then also refuses a source outside the package's directories.","summary":"//web:dist_sdk takes all of :files_app, so a shell, extension or quickstart edit rebuilds the package and reruns its tests, and the graph leaves the package boundary to the license guard alone","tags":["review","review:pr45-client-split","bazel","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:42:08.441960Z","id":"1f33b0396670c5339b8c0d47ca66891e656185f963a6f8325f0d732c5bedb04f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1fc4437b2","summary":"web/BUILD.bazel: files_sdk (sdk/**, overlay/**, bridge/** without tests, build-sdk.mjs, extension-clean.mjs, overlay-component-css.mjs, package.json, svelte.config.js, tsconfig.json) is the only source input of //web:dist_sdk; files_app is files_sdk plus files_app_rest. //web:dist_sdk builds and //web:sdk_package and //web:bundle_size pass (bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error //web/... //scripts/...: 40 tests pass).","supersedes":"b9e393f8335c7beb5df7ab38931734e4701593f06f10f0114498596b79af3dd8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-02T20:43:12.176348Z","id":"371dc027c5d4f7a12beb8cf31b8a6046610a4d2e25da8952c19aa2e9f2c2d7d8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f5994fc4db006bb8b01da2c9d41fd690541a7237","summary":"web/BUILD.bazel: files_sdk (sdk/**, overlay/**, bridge/** without tests, build-sdk.mjs, extension-clean.mjs, overlay-component-css.mjs, package.json, svelte.config.js, tsconfig.json) is the only source input of //web:dist_sdk; files_app is files_sdk plus files_app_rest. //web:dist_sdk builds and //web:sdk_package and //web:bundle_size pass (bazelisk test --lockfile_mode=error //web/... //scripts/...: 40 tests pass).","supersedes":"1f33b0396670c5339b8c0d47ca66891e656185f963a6f8325f0d732c5bedb04f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/playwright.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T18:59:10.284462Z","id":"2bec3cb4592451f12d461ca8961aec838fc077151f9fe61e3374c09862fec743","body":{"detail":"`expect.timeout` is WAIT_MS (110 s; 5 s on origin/main) and the test timeout is HANG_MS (120 s; 30 s on origin/main). CI gives each of //web:e2e_gesture, //web:e2e_chrome_overlay, //web:e2e_queues and //web:e2e_rest 300 s for its whole run (`test:ci --test_timeout=300`, .bazelrc:110) on 8 workers (CLAX_E2E_WORKERS in web/BUILD.bazel): 2,400 worker-seconds, of which each failing expectation takes 110. A change that breaks one shared control and fails about twenty tests (fewer, once the passing tests' own time is counted) ends as a Bazel TIMEOUT; Playwright's list reporter prints the errors in its end-of-run summary, so that summary is lost, where origin/main reported each such failure after 5 s. The comment here says a stuck test 'is reported by Playwright, not cut off with the rest of the run': that holds for one or two stuck tests, not for a broken build. web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts:32 sets its own HANG_MS of 300_000, the whole CI limit, so a stuck test there is always cut off by Bazel first. Neither this config nor the Bazel targets set maxFailures or globalTimeout.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"5784818ad7319aad39fb953814a4a3e3ea01014d92a0548b3a37ae73044e25d9"},"suggested_fix":"Under Bazel set `maxFailures` to about the worker count, so a broken build ends the run after its first round of failures and prints them; or set `globalTimeout` a little under the Bazel limit as the run's own hang guard, so Playwright ends the run and prints its summary itself. Bring chrome-overlay's HANG_MS under the CI limit (or give //web:e2e_chrome_overlay a longer Bazel timeout), and say in the comment how many stuck tests the limit covers.","summary":"A never-met expectation now holds its worker for 110 s, so a handful of failures uses up CI's 300 s target limit before Playwright reports them","tags":["review","review:deterministic-tests-2026-11-12","session:claude-code:82c42a10-6c82-42ed-a424-ae8ec2a814c7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/playwright.config.ts","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T19:02:42.080651Z","id":"31bd403b7d0ef371861e0ff56b475866d1e72a6eb34d508f99e03826c66569e4","body":{"detail":"web/playwright.config.ts:29-30 and 37-38: `timeout: HANG_MS` (120_000), `expect: { timeout: WAIT_MS }` (110_000); `git show origin/main:web/playwright.config.ts` lines 26-27: `timeout: 30_000`, `expect: { timeout: 5_000 }`. .bazelrc:110: `test:ci --test_timeout=300`. web/BUILD.bazel:400: `CLAX_E2E_WORKERS: \"8\"` on every e2e_* target. 300 s x 8 workers = 2,400 worker-seconds, 21 waits of 110 s. `git grep -n 'maxFailures\\|globalTimeout\\|printFailuresInline\\|PLAYWRIGHT_LIST_PRINT' -- . ':!*.qual'` prints nothing. What a Bazel timeout loses: bazel/js/npm_script.mjs:107-118 answers SIGTERM by sending SIGKILL to the script's process group, and playwright 1.63.0's list reporter (web/node_modules/.pnpm/playwright@1.63.0/node_modules/playwright/lib/runner/index.js, ListReporter.onTestEnd and onEnd) writes a failure's error only in onEnd's epilogue unless printFailuresInline is set; its runner handles SIGINT only. The one-line rows of tests that had already ended are printed as they end, so their names survive; their errors do not. Two parts are older than the branch: chrome-overlay's 300 s test limit (origin/main:web/e2e/chrome-overlay.spec.ts:30, `TEST_MS = 300_000`, now HANG_MS at line 32) and CI's 300 s (origin/main:.bazelrc:103). Outside CI the targets get Bazel's `long` timeout (bazel/js/defs.bzl:55), so the limit bites in CI only. The kind is right: a risk to how a broken build is reported, not a failing test.","kind":"comment","references":"2bec3cb4592451f12d461ca8961aec838fc077151f9fe61e3374c09862fec743","summary":"confirmed: an unmet expectation waits 110 s where origin/main's waited 5 s, CI ends a target at 300 s on 8 workers, and a run Bazel ends prints no error text","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:82c42a10-6c82-42ed-a424-ae8ec2a814c7"]}}
